Pre-adapter that runs before upstream's `all_of_them.patch` so the
upstream patch can apply verbatim against the haybarn engine fork.

The only point where the haybarn engine's source diverges from
upstream DuckDB v1.5.2 inside the region upstream's patch touches is
the rebranded error message in `extension_load.cpp`. Upstream's patch
has the original "DuckDB extensions are files..." as a removal-context
line; the haybarn engine says "Haybarn extensions are files...".
Without this pre-adapter, `patch` can't find that line and the hunk
(which removes the entire EndsWith check from the wasm-loadable path)
fails to apply.

We just temporarily rebrand back to "DuckDB" for that one line.
Upstream's patch then deletes the line entirely (the wasm-loadable
path doesn't need a filename-suffix gatekeeper since the whole flow
is replaced by in-memory fetch + signature validation), so the
"DuckDB" wording never actually reaches a runtime binary or user.

If/when upstream's patch is reworked or the haybarn engine reroutes
that error string through a different code path, this adapter
becomes a no-op and can be deleted.

diff --git a/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp b/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
--- a/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
+++ b/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
@@ -454,7 +454,7 @@
 	if (!StringUtil::EndsWith(filename, ".duckdb_extension")) {
 		throw PermissionException(
-		    "Haybarn extensions are files ending with '.duckdb_extension', loading different "
+		    "DuckDB extensions are files ending with '.duckdb_extension', loading different "
 		    "files is not possible, error while loading from '%s', consider 'INSTALL <path>; LOAD <name>;'",
 		    filename);
 	}

